HST Office: OLE objects whose preview is vector data (the WMF/EMF Word stores for MathType,
Equation 3.0, ChemDraw, ChemWindow objects) were drawn on screen with Graphic::Draw, which
renders the vector graphic into a bitmap of the painted pixel size and blits it. Formulas
looked blurry next to the body text, most visibly at high zoom and on scaled displays, and
on some backends the glyphs were lost. Print and PDF export already painted them as
primitives. Screen painting now does the same, through one HST helper used for every
output (sw/source/core/hst/olereplacementpaint.cxx).

